  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Opening Crowd Noise**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **Crying on Eddie Nash's Grave**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 6 archived performances [2]\n- **Cadaver Sniffing Dog**: back after 77 archived shows (1097 days) [2]\n- **First verse of \"Make a Circuit With Me\" by The Polecats (Cover)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **Song for Layne Staley**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 6 archived performances [2]\n- **Charlie Sheen Reaches Out to the Feds**: rare: 14 archived performances [2]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tmg2026-08-10** (recommended): source not stated; 13 songs; 50 min [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: Andrew Eldritch, Hot Girl Shallow Grave Summer, Wurster's Drumpad [1]\n- Band played a shorter, sweatier set at West Seattle's Easy Street Records after a larger ZooTunes show [1]\n- Wurster used a drumpad, and all three members stood in a horizontal line on the small stage [1]\n- The store was packed, with the crowd stretching around the block before entry began [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **tmg2026-08-10**: source: iPhone [1]",
